<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If I described this moment to myself by name, what would I tell me to do next?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "From a colleague's seat, how much of this meeting is actually about me?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I replaying this slip in the first person, and what would an observer say mattered instead?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I turned the distanced view into one concrete next action?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "Priya, picture this from the back of the room: eight people focused on their own slides. You spotted a real gap. Ask one short question about the churn assumption, then let the lead answer." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "I'm going to sound naive. Everyone will remember that I'm the one who didn't get the model. I'll just keep quiet and email the lead later." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "An analyst is about to raise a concern about a vendor's numbers in a cross-team review where she is the most junior person." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "Naming herself and taking an observer's view shrinks the imagined spotlight and turns vague dread into one specific, low-cost contribution, which is the pattern lab studies link to less distress and better performance." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Before the meeting or talk, write or say two or three sentences of self-talk using your own name or \"you\" instead of \"I\" (for example, \"Sam, you know this material; your job is to explain it\")." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Picture the room from the back row or from a colleague's seat, not through your own eyes, and ask what that observer would actually notice." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Notice what the observer is busy with - their own agenda, notes and next point - and adjust your estimate of how much attention you will get." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Turn the distanced view into one concrete action, such as the opening line, the one question you will ask or the one-sentence correction you will use if you slip." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Afterwards, review the moment the same way (\"What did Sam do well? What would Sam change?\") instead of replaying it in the first person." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Self-distancing strategies" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Self-distancing strategies" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "distanced self-talk" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "observer-perspective imagery" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "self-distancing" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "third-person self-talk" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/emotion-regulation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Stepping back from your own point of view before or after a nerve-racking moment - by talking to yourself by name or as \"you\", or by picturing the scene as an outside observer would - so that you judge the stakes and your own salience more like the audience does." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/barriers-and-psychology> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Self-distancing strategies" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/illusion-of-transparency> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mindfulness> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/presentation-rehearsal> .
