  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s4> <https://schema.org/url> <https://core.ac.uk/download/300057876.pdf> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "Journal of Anxiety Disorders 21(6), 804-819, 2007 (PubMed record)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "The spotlight effect and the illusion of transparency in social anxiety" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#sourceType> "peer-reviewed" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s5> <https://schema.org/url> <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17166695/> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I staying quiet because I think everyone will remember this one comment, when they are mostly thinking about their own contributions?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If a colleague had made the slip I just made, would I still be thinking about it tomorrow?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I about to spend the first minute of my talk apologising for something the audience has not noticed?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If I picture this meeting from the back of the room instead of through my own eyes, how big does my moment really look?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Barrier> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Spotlight effect" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "overestimating how much others notice us" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "spotlighting" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/egocentric-bias> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The tendency to overestimate how much other people notice, remember and judge our appearance, words and slip-ups, which makes communicators hold back, over-apologise and dwell on small mistakes that the audience barely registered." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/barriers-and-psychology> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Spotlight effect" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/curse-of-knowledge> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/illusion-of-transparency> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/speaking-anxiety> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/spotlight-effect/s5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#causes> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-anxiety> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#confusedWith> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/illusion-of-transparency> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#demonstratedBy> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/gilovich-kruger-medvec-2002> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#demonstratedBy> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/gilovich-medvec-savitsky-2000> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#domain> "barriers-and-psychology" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#evidenceStatus> "mixed" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#explainedBy> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anchoring-and-adjustment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#file> "articles/barriers-and-psychology/spotlight-effect.md" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#level> "introductory" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#supportedBy> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/macrae-et-al-2016> .
}

<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Could someone who disagrees with me still accept my description of what happened as accurate?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I written down more than one explanation, including one that would make this behaviour sensible where they come from?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which of my own norms am I using to judge this, and where did I learn it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I about to give feedback that starts with my verdict instead of what I observed?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "In the last three reviews you didn't comment during the meeting, then emailed me concerns afterwards - and they were good ones. I can think of a few reasons that might happen. How do design disagreements usually get raised on teams you've worked on?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "You're not engaging in reviews. If you disagree, say it in the room - sending emails afterwards looks like you're going around the team." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead in a global project notices that a newly transferred engineer never raises objections in design reviews and later sends concerns privately by email." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The first version presents an evaluation (\"not engaging\", \"going around the team\") as fact; the second states the observable pattern, admits several possible explanations and asks before judging, so the engineer can explain a norm the lead may not share." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "When a colleague's behaviour surprises or irritates you, pause before replying and write down only what you saw or heard, in words a camera could confirm." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "List at least two or three different explanations for that behaviour, including at least one that would make it reasonable in the other person's context." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Name your own evaluation and its source - what you feel about the behaviour and which norm you are measuring it against." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Check the most important explanation with the person or a cultural informant using a neutral question built on your description." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Only then decide how to respond, and if you give feedback, lead with the description rather than the evaluation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Describe-analyze-evaluate" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Describe-analyze-evaluate" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "D.A.E." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "D.I.E. model" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "DAE model" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "DIE exercise" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "describe-interpret-evaluate" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "description-interpretation-evaluation" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/intercultural-communication> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A three-step habit for unfamiliar or puzzling behaviour: first describe only what you observed, then list several possible explanations, and only then notice your own evaluation, so that a culture-bound judgement does not masquerade as a fact." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/cross-cultural-communication> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Describe-analyze-evaluate" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/direct-vs-indirect-feedback> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/ethnocentrism> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/ladder-of-inference> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/describe-analyze-evaluate/s1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/describe-analyze-evaluate/s2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/describe-analyze-evaluate/s3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/describe-analyze-evaluate/s4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/describe-analyze-evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/describe-analyze-evaluate/s5> .
