  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/defensiveness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "defensive reaction" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/defensiveness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "getting defensive" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/defensiveness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communication-climate> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/defensiveness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A self-protective reaction to perceived or anticipated threat in a conversation, in which a person spends energy guarding their image instead of taking in the message - and in which the listener's distorted hearing tends to make the speaker defensive in turn." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/defensiveness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/difficult-conversations-and-conflict> .
