<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I said out loud, or written in the invite, whether cameras are expected in this meeting and why?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would a new team member feel safe turning their camera off here, and have I told them so?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I modelling the norm, or does my own always-on camera quietly signal that video is required?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When cameras are off, do I still give everyone a clear way to contribute?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "Team charter line - 'Stand-up: cameras optional. Planning: cameras on for the first 10 minutes of check-in, optional after. 1:1s: your call.' The lead turns their own camera off after the check-in, calls on people by name, and tells new joiners in their first 1:1 that cameras-off is normal here." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Invite text - 'Cameras on please, it helps us stay connected.' The lead keeps a full gallery view, comments when a tile is dark, and the newest analysts never switch off even on their fourth call of the day." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead runs a daily 30-minute stand-up and two weekly hour-long planning calls for eight people, several of whom joined in the last three months." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The expectation is explicit and tied to the purpose of each meeting, the lead's behaviour shows the norm is real, and the people under the most self-presentation pressure hear it said to them directly, while the check-in keeps the group connection that buffers fatigue." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "List your recurring video meetings and decide for each whether faces add value - small working sessions, sensitive one-to-ones and first meetings with new people usually benefit; large updates, webinars and long all-hands rarely do." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Agree the camera expectation for each meeting type with the team, write it in the invite or team charter, and say plainly that cameras-off is fine wherever video is not needed." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Tell newer colleagues directly, in person or one-to-one, that turning the camera off will not count against them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Model it as the organiser - switch your own camera off for part of a long meeting or for audio-only segments, because people follow what they see others doing." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Keep participation visible without video - ask people by name, use chat, reactions or a shared document, and agree that cameras-off still means no multitasking." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "When video is used, suggest hiding self-view once framing is set, and build in short audio-only breaks in meetings longer than about 45 minutes." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Camera-optional norm" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Camera-optional norm" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "camera-optional meetings" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "cameras-optional policy" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "video-off option" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/meeting-norms> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An explicit team agreement that webcams are a choice rather than a requirement in video meetings, set per meeting type and modelled by the person running the meeting, so people can rest from being on camera without being judged for it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/digital-and-async-communication> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Camera-optional norm" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/channel-selection> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/spotlight-effect> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/workplace-meetings> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/camera-optional-norm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/zoom-fatigue> .
