<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I given a number or range where I have one, instead of a word like \"probably\" or \"should be fine\"?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I said separately how good the evidence behind my estimate is?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I told them what we do not yet know, what we are doing to find out and when we will know?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I presenting real disagreement among experts or data as such, rather than smoothing it over or overplaying it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is the uncertainty in the sentence that carries the estimate, not in a footnote or a later slide?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "Our best estimate is that 3% of accounts cancel in the first quarter, with a plausible range of 1-6%. The estimate rests on a four-week pilot in one region, so confidence is moderate. We will know much more after the second region's renewals on 15 March; until then I'd budget for 6%." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Churn should be fine - we don't expect much impact, though obviously nobody can be sure." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A product lead tells the leadership team how many customers a pricing change will cost." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The before version mixes false reassurance with a blanket hedge, so leaders can neither plan nor challenge it; the after version gives a point estimate, a range, the quality of the evidence and when it will improve, which is what a decision needs." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Skill> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Communicating uncertainty to decision makers" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "conveying what is and is not known" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "expressing uncertainty" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "uncertainty communication" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/risk-communication> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The skill of telling the people who must decide what you know, how precisely you know it, how solid the evidence is and what you are doing to learn more - stated as specifically as your knowledge allows rather than hidden, hedged into vagueness or inflated into false certainty." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/executive-and-client-communication> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Communicating uncertainty to decision makers" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/bottom-line-up-front> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/credibility> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/delivering-bad-news> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/illusion-of-transparency> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/communicating-uncertainty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/managing-up> .
