<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Concept> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Feedback" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "feedback interventions" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "performance feedback" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "workplace feedback" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/interpersonal-communication> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Information given to a person about their performance or understanding, relative to a goal, so they can close the gap; on average it improves performance, but a sizeable share of feedback makes things worse, depending mainly on what it draws attention to and how much usable information it carries." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/feedback-and-coaching> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Feedback" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/defensiveness> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/direct-vs-indirect-feedback> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/one-on-one-meetings> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/performance-review> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/receiving-feedback> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact> .
