<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I named one behaviour I want to improve in the future, rather than asking for a verdict on the past?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When a suggestion arrived, did I say \"thank you\" - or did I explain why it would not work?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I using feedforward to avoid a conversation about a real problem that still needs to be discussed?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which of the suggestions will I actually try, and have I told the people who gave them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "I'm working on running kick-offs that finish on time. Could you give me two ideas I could try at the next one? I'll just note them down - no need to go back over last week." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Can you give me some feedback on last week's kick-off? I know it ran 40 minutes over, but the client kept raising scope questions, so honestly I'm not sure what I could have done differently." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A project manager whose kick-off meetings regularly overrun wants to improve before the next quarter's projects start." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The first version invites a debate about a past meeting and opens with a defence, so the colleague has to argue to be helpful; the rewrite names a future goal, asks for a bounded number of ideas and promises not to argue, which makes it easy to offer useful suggestions." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Pick one specific behaviour you want to get better at, phrased as a future goal (\"run tighter project kick-offs\"), not a past failure." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Describe that goal briefly to a colleague who has seen you work or who knows the subject - they do not need to be your manager." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask for two concrete suggestions for the future, and make clear you are not asking for a review of anything that already happened." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Listen and write the suggestions down without judging, explaining or defending - the only permitted reply is \"thank you\"." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Offer to return the favour - ask what they want to improve and give them two forward-looking suggestions in turn." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Repeat with a few different people, then choose the suggestions you will actually try and tell those colleagues what you changed." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Feedforward" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Feedforward" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "feed-forward" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "future-focused feedback" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "try feedforward instead of feedback" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedback> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A development technique popularised by executive coach Marshall Goldsmith: instead of reviewing what someone did wrong, you name one behaviour you want to improve and ask others for a couple of concrete suggestions for the future, which you listen to and thank them for without debate." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/feedforward> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/feedback-and-coaching> .
