<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Could I state their point, and how they feel about it, well enough that they would say \"yes, exactly\"?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I hold back advice, reassurance and my own counter-argument until they confirmed I understood?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Was my attention on them, or was I rehearsing my reply or glancing at a screen?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I ask at least one question that drew out something they had not yet said?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would they leave this conversation feeling heard, even if I did not agree with them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Skill> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Active listening" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Rogerian listening" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "empathic listening" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "high-quality listening" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/listening> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The learnable skill of listening to understand another person's full meaning - the content and the feeling behind it - and showing that understanding back to them, while holding off judgment, advice and persuasion until they confirm you have understood." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/listening> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/active-listening> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Active listening" .
