<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is my question specific enough that people could write concrete answers to it on their own?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I protect the silent-writing and round-robin phases from early debate or evaluation, including my own?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did each person rank privately, so seniors' preferences were not visible before others voted?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is this really a single-question, prioritise-and-decide meeting, or does the topic need open exploration first?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "Take ten minutes and write down, on your own, every process problem that slows you down. Then we'll go round the table one idea at a time, I'll number them, and everyone ranks their top five privately before we talk priorities." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Okay, open floor - what should we fix first? ... Great point, Sam [senior lead], the ticketing tool is a mess. Anyone disagree? No? Let's go with that." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "An operations manager runs a one-hour meeting with eight team members, including two senior leads, to decide which process problems to fix first next quarter." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The open floor lets the first senior voice anchor the room and blocks quieter people from offering ideas; silent writing and private ranking let every member contribute and weigh in equally before status and conversation shape the outcome." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Write one specific, open question on the board or shared screen and read it aloud, for example \"What are the biggest obstacles to closing month-end two days faster?\"" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Give everyone 10-20 minutes of silent, individual writing to list as many answers as they can, with no talking." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Run a round robin - each person reads out one idea per turn, which you record verbatim and number - and keep going until the lists are exhausted; allow no debate yet." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Walk through the numbered list for clarification only, letting anyone explain an item, and merge true duplicates with the agreement of the people who raised them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask each person to privately pick and rank their top five items (5 points for the most important down to 1), then tally the scores in front of the group." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Discuss the top-ranked items and the surprises in the tally, and, if the scores are close, run a second private vote before you commit to next steps." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Nominal group technique" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Nominal group technique" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "NGT" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "nominal group process" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/facilitation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/group-decision-making> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A structured meeting method for generating and prioritising ideas in which people first write ideas silently and alone, then share them one at a time in a round robin, clarify them, and finally rank them privately so the group's priorities come from pooled individual votes." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/meetings-and-facilitation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nominal-group-technique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Nominal group technique" .
