<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Phenomenon> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Psychological safety" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "interpersonal risk-taking climate" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "team psychological safety" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/team-climate> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A shared belief among members of a team that it is safe to take interpersonal risks - to ask a question, admit a mistake, raise a concern or disagree - without being embarrassed, rejected or punished for it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/meetings-and-facilitation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/psychological-safety> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Psychological safety" .
