<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do I know the likely range of agreement better than, as well as, or worse than the other side?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is my opening based on my target and a reason I can say out loud, rather than on my walk-away point?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is it ambitious enough to leave room to move but not so extreme that it could offend or end the talks?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I about to reveal a preference we probably share, which they could trade back to me as a concession?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If they opened first, have I re-anchored on my own numbers before replying?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "Based on the three proposals we reviewed for similar scope, we'd like to propose $8,500 a month for six months, with the weekly dashboard and quarterly review included. That reflects the market and a six-month commitment from us. How does that sit with you?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "We don't have a fixed budget yet - what would you normally charge for something like this?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A marketing team lead is buying a six-month analytics retainer from a small agency she has researched; similar retainers she found ranged from $8K to $11K a month." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "She knows the market range at least as well as the agency, so moving first lets her set the reference point near the low end with a stated rationale, instead of inviting the agency to anchor at the top of the range." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Before the conversation, research the market and estimate the zone of possible agreement - your walk-away point, the other side's likely walk-away point, and what comparable deals settled at." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Decide whether to move first - do so when you know the range at least as well as the other side; if they clearly know more, ask questions and let them open." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Set the offer from your ambitious target, not from your walk-away point, and make sure it is one you can justify with a real reason." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Limit the opening to the issues where your interests conflict; hold back terms you suspect both sides want anyway until you have learned their preferences." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "State the number precisely and confidently, give the reason in one or two sentences, then stop talking and listen." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "If they open first, do not respond to their number straight away - restate your own target, their likely limits and your alternatives to yourself, then counter from your plan rather than from their anchor." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "First offer" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "First offer" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "anchoring in negotiation" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "first-mover advantage" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "first-offer effect" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "making the first offer" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "opening offer" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/distributive-negotiation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Deliberately naming the opening number or package in a negotiation so that it anchors the other side's expectations, and deciding - based on who knows more about the zone of possible agreement - whether to move first at all and how ambitious to be." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/negotiation> .
