<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Concept> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mehrabian's 7-38-55 rule" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "7%-38%-55% rule" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "7-38-55 rule" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "93% nonverbal myth" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Mehrabian myth" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "communication is 93% nonverbal" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/nonverbal-communication> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The popular claim that only 7% of a message's meaning comes from words, 38% from tone of voice and 55% from facial expression and body language; it overgeneralises two narrow 1967 lab studies about inconsistent cues for liking, and Mehrabian himself says it does not apply to communication in general." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/nonverbal-and-voice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Mehrabian's 7-38-55 rule" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/channel-selection> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/facial-expressions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mixed-messages> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/paralanguage> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/proxemics> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/mehrabian-myth/s1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/mehrabian-myth/s2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/mehrabian-myth> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/mehrabian-myth/s3> .
