<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Can I state in one sentence which of leadership's existing goals this issue helps, and is that link honest?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I bringing a proposed solution and the evidence my leaders usually ask for, or only a complaint?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who else have I involved, and would any of them be surprised to hear me raise it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is this the right moment and forum, or am I raising it because I am frustrated right now?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If they say no, what will I do next - and am I prepared to accept that answer?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "Proposal for Thursday's ops review: about a third of last month's support tickets trace to the billing page. A two-sprint redesign, already scoped with product, would cut handling costs and supports this year's customer-retention goal. I'd like a decision on adding it to Q1. One-page case attached; finance has checked the numbers." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Hi all, I wanted to flag (again) that the billing page is a mess. My team is drowning in tickets and nobody seems to care. Can we please prioritise this?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A support team lead wants leadership to fund a fix for a confusing billing page that drives a large share of tickets." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The rewrite ties the issue to a goal leaders own, brings data and a solution, shows peers are already involved, and uses a scheduled forum - the packaging, involvement and process moves the research links to success - instead of venting frustration." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Write the issue in one sentence and link it to a goal, metric or priority your leaders already own, framed as an opportunity where honestly possible." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Find out how the decision maker likes to receive proposals - data or story, a written pre-read or a conversation - and what evidence counts in your organisation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Build a short business case - cost, benefit, risk and what happens if nothing changes - and bring at least one concrete proposed solution, not only the problem." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Test the idea with peers and one or two respected senior people first; fold in their objections and ask who should be involved or informed." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Read the context before you raise it - is leadership listening, under pressure, or recently burned by a similar idea? - and pick a moment and channel that fit." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Raise it calmly, acknowledge any past decision you are revisiting without blaming whoever made it, and ask for one specific next step." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/7> <https://schema.org/position> "7"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/7> <https://schema.org/text> "Follow up, report what happened, and decide deliberately whether to persist, re-bundle the issue with another priority, or let it go for now." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Selling issues to leadership" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling/howto/7> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Selling issues to leadership" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "getting the boss to buy in" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "issue selling" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "selling ideas upward" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/persuasion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Deliberately getting senior leaders to notice, understand and act on an issue, idea or risk you see from below - by framing it in terms of goals they already own, involving allies, and choosing the timing and channel - as described in Jane E. Dutton and Susan J. Ashford's research on issue selling." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/issue-selling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/persuasion-and-influence> .
