  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s4> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Surprising but true: Half the decisions in organizations fail" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#sourceType> "peer-reviewed" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s4> <https://schema.org/url> <https://cebma.org/assets/Uploads/Nutt-1999-gecomprimeerd.pdf> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "University of Essex, Strategic Project Delivery staff guidance" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Stakeholder analysis and communications plan" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#sourceType> "institutional" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/stakeholder-mapping/s5> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.essex.ac.uk/staff/strategic-project-delivery/stakeholder-analysis-comms-plan> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who could stop or slow this, and have I spoken to them directly rather than assuming their view?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who will be most affected but has the least say, and how will they hear about it before it lands?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does each group's message answer their concern, or is it the same message I would send everyone?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When did I last update this map, and has anyone's stance or influence changed since?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "Map: Finance director (high power, high interest, undecided) - weekly check-in, co-own the cut-over date. Payroll lead (high power, low interest) - one briefing on the export file, sign-off by week 3. Frequent travellers in sales (low power, high interest, worried about slower refunds) - invite two to test in week 2, answer the refund-time question in every message. Everyone else - short email at go-live and a two-minute video." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Plan: send one all-staff email two weeks before go-live announcing the new tool, with a link to the user guide." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "An operations manager is replacing the team's expense-claims tool and has a go-live date in six weeks." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The single email treated everyone as one audience; the map shows who can block the launch, who will feel it most and what each needs to hear, so the manager spends attention where a surprise would be costly." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Write down the decision or change in one sentence and set the boundary - which teams, customers, regulators and time frame are in scope." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "List everyone who can affect it or will be affected by it, then ask two or three colleagues outside your team who is missing, including people with little voice." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "For each stakeholder, note their main interest or concern, whether they currently support, oppose or are undecided, and what power they hold (budget, sign-off, expertise, reputation, ability to block)." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Place each one on a power-versus-interest grid and pick an engagement level - partner closely, keep satisfied, consult, or keep informed." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "For each group, decide who will talk to them, the one message that speaks to their interest, the channel and how often - then put that in a communication plan." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Test the map by talking to the stakeholders themselves, and revisit it at each milestone, because power, interest and stance shift." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Stakeholder mapping" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Stakeholder mapping" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "influence-interest matrix" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "power-interest grid" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "stakeholder analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "stakeholder map" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/persuasion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A planning technique for listing everyone who can affect or is affected by a decision or change, sorting them by how much power and interest they have, and using that picture to decide whom to involve, consult or inform, and with what message." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/stakeholder-mapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/persuasion-and-influence> .
