<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I trying to force myself to feel calm, or accepting that being keyed up is normal before something that matters?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What is one thing that could go well in this talk, and have I pointed my energy at it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I using the reframe as a substitute for preparing and rehearsing out loud?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "After the talk, am I judging it by what the audience did, or by how nervous I felt?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "My heart's racing because this matters - that's energy I can use. I'm excited to show them why the logistics overspend is a one-off and get the forecast approved." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Calm down, calm down. They'll see I'm nervous. Just get through the slides without messing up." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A finance analyst is about to present a quarterly variance review to the leadership team for the first time and notices her hands shaking in the corridor." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The first version fights the arousal, which rarely works, and keeps attention on what could go wrong. The second accepts the arousal, labels it as excitement and points it at a concrete opportunity - the shift the reappraisal studies tested." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Expect your heart rate, breathing and alertness to rise before the talk, and stop treating that as proof that something is wrong." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Remind yourself, in a sentence, what the arousal is for - it moves oxygen and attention to where you need them for the task." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Just before you start, say \"I am excited\" (aloud or under your breath) instead of telling yourself to calm down." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Turn the excitement toward the opportunity - name one thing that could go well, such as the decision you want the audience to make." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Pair the reframe with preparation and rehearsal; it changes how the nerves feel, not whether you know your material." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Afterwards, judge the talk by what the audience understood or decided, not by how anxious you felt." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Anxiety reappraisal" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Anxiety reappraisal" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "arousal reappraisal" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "excitement reappraisal" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "get-excited reframe" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "reappraising anxiety as excitement" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Reinterpreting the racing heart and jitters before a talk, interview or other evaluated performance as useful energy or excitement - rather than trying to calm down - so that the arousal is treated as a resource for the task instead of a sign of threat." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/presenting-and-public-speaking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anxiety-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Anxiety reappraisal" .
