<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I ask at least one question I did not already know the answer to?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Was my question a real question, or a suggestion or a test dressed up as one?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who talked more in that conversation, and did I learn anything that changed my view?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I acknowledge what they said before telling them what I think?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "You built this differently from our usual deck - I'd like to understand why. Can you walk me through what you were going for and what you know about this client that I might not?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "This isn't the template we use. Please redo it in the standard deck format tonight so we're ready for tomorrow." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead notices a direct report delivered a client analysis in an unexpected format, a day before the client review." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The first version assumes the lead already knows everything relevant and shuts the report down; the second surfaces their reasoning (perhaps the client asked for it), keeps them engaged, and still leaves time to agree a format together." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Before the conversation, write down what you are assuming about the situation and the person, and mark which parts you have not actually checked." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Open with a question you do not know the answer to (\"Walk me through how you approached this\") instead of your verdict or fix." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Stop after the question and let the other person talk; resist filling the first silence with your own view." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask one genuine follow-up that builds on what they just said, rather than steering back to your agenda." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Acknowledge what you heard in your own words before you add any opinion, request or decision." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Only then tell - share your view or ask for what you need - and invite them to correct or add to it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/humble-inquiry/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
